    {
      "id": "38408ea8727214282b736cc2b4ed92d0d0068357",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1609394589,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The \"Windows Build\" pipeline job tests are failing with \"returned non-zero exit status 3221225781\", which translates to Windows error c0000135, which suggests a missing DLL.\n\nIf I build manually in a container on the MR builder, I don't get any 3221225781 / c0000135 failures. Most of the tests pass but each executable prints\n\n```\n ** (tshark:6212) 17:12:51.637677 [GLib WARNING] -- Failed to determine console output code page: The system could not find the environment option that was entered.. Falling back to UTF-8\n```\n\nprior to printing anything else. Running `chcp` returns\n\n```\nActive code page: 0\n```\n\nTests work fine in my local VM, and commands don't show the code page warning.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789689689",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-10-18T17:44:04.781Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-10-18T19:11:27.922Z",
